Galzu is a tengu of [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]], the sister of [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and one of three children of [[People/Adal|Adal]]. She worked alongside her grandmother, and was the most driven of the three. Her feathers are mostly black, with blue at the tips of the longer ones, and she never cared for pink bows. Her eyes carry a faint yellow glow now that was not there when her brother knew her.

She spent months talking with the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]] in [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]]. She argued with her father and stormed out of the roost, and for a long time was not seen again. Her disappearance came at the same time as a break-in at a Belvedere archival facility. Adal searched her room afterward and found nothing out of place.

She turned up aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], in Neweth, the town around the heart [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Tally|Tally]], one of four tengu who rarely leave one another's company. [[People/Egan Arithmites|Egan]] counts her among a later, more fervent wave of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]]'s followers. She worked a rite to wake the dead Heart, pouring magic into it from the inner sanctum above. She came ready to fight and could still cast where sound is killed, and she held out until she was beaten down. She was lucid through all of it, and no spell of the mind held her.

The Party took her alive and tried to enter her mind to break the Herald's hold. Her defenses were past them: a black layer with no light in it over a pit of centipedes her own mind had made, and beneath that a mind they could not reach. The only way to weaken her, they learned, is to weaken the god's hold on her. She is held unconscious in a blue suspension chamber at [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Lifeline|Lifeline]], in the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Machine God|Machine God]]'s Undercroft. The chamber feeds her power as it keeps her, and the Party has a few weeks to move the strider before she grows past any hope of reaching her mind.
